    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for the Austin Waves is characterized by a lean toward efficiency as we navigate late-season game caps. **Kyle Tucker** emerges as our most reliable asset, yielding a strong score of 61.84. Despite a neutral matchup against Kerr and the inherent suppression of a lefty-lefty dynamic, **Kyle Tucker**\u2019s pedigree and elite consistency keep him locked in the starting outfield. While **Andy Pages** (53.60) and **Jackson Merrill** (49.86) land in the marginal-to-strong territory, **Jackson Merrill** remains a high-upside play; although he faces a tough 3.14 xERA from Henderson, his specific profile as a speed-first asset\u2014carrying a 40% SB indicator\u2014provides the necessary category support we prioritize in our 5x5 Roto construction.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the marginal edge given to **Andy Pages** over our deeper bench options. While **Drake Baldwin** earns a 47.91 score leading off against Snell, his offensive output is capped by a difficult 3.22 xERA matchup. The optimizer heavily favored the stability of our outfield trio over the volatility of bench assets like **Heliot Ramos** or **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, both of whom were excluded to preserve remaining games for high-leverage opportunities later in the week. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** are sidelined due to today\u2019s schedule, while our long-term concerns persist with **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remaining on the IL. We are proceeding with caution as we monitor the lineup security of **Drake Baldwin**, whose score assumes the top-of-the-order protection despite the high-caliber arm of Snell on the mound.",
